# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf.
#
# This repo was written on macOS and is now developed on Windows as well, where
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true by default. That makes the same
# checkout behave differently per OS: text files arrive CRLF on Windows and LF
# on macOS. Nothing breaks today (the index is all LF, and autocrlf normalizes
# on commit), but it means correctness depends on a setting nobody chose, and a
# contributor whose autocrlf is false would commit CRLF over the whole tree.
#
# Normalize to LF in the repository; let checkouts use their platform's ending
# for everything, except the shell scripts.
* text=auto

# A CRLF shebang is fatal, not cosmetic: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the
# script fail with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" the moment it
# runs on macOS, WSL or Git Bash. Keep the Unix scripts LF on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
